llowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-16T10:30:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T10:30:26Z","body":"In my opinion it would be reasonable to have the highlight whenever you mouse over any part of the (disabled) section, for consistency with the other (enabled) sections, and (to solve the OP's issue) to make it easy to see which checkbox belongs to the section. I think it would also be reasonable if clicking on the section name still did nothing (or would briefly highlight the checkbox), since it's like the action of unfolding an empty section. It might be very mildly unexpected the first time you try it, but you'd understand it afterward. (And as mentioned before the performance implications of enabling a section are a good reason not to enable the checkbox just by clicking the section.)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3077945633/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3078177216","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108625#issuecomment-3078177216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108625","